   "id": "wait-response",
   "topic": "Network and API",
   "lv": "h",
   "q": "How do you check that clicking \"Place order\" sends the right request?",
   "hint": "Wait for the request or response around the click, then inspect it.",
   "answer": "Start <code>page.waitForResponse</code> (or <code>waitForRequest</code>) with a URL or predicate before the click, then check the status and the JSON body after it.",
   "explain": "<p>Starting the wait after the click can miss a fast response, so create the promise first and await it after. Python uses <code>with page.expect_response(...) as info</code> and Java uses <code>page.waitForResponse(predicate, () -&gt; ...)</code>.</p>",
